{sin}⁡(Bx+C)+D,$ the period is $\\frac{{360}^{∘}}{B}.$\n\nIn our case, we have that $B=\\frac{4}{3}.$ Therefore, the period is $\\frac{{360}^{∘}}{(\\frac{4}{3})}={270}^{∘}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-117579/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1eeb42af-74ee-53d7-af9f-be171f77968f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-117579"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-236890/selection/d5383cc560f7210ce951b287d42180f2c52a051d33d7310f4c07703ce1cd1b4e" :answer/id #uuid "b0a7334e-2881-537b-973e-09c8ab166460" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-236890/selection/dbaf85835946aefb97564ba0d1ea287b684a4c8821f4256502e349376df74d28" :answer/id #uuid "05f916aa-39c6-5a56-b4df-c5a7f6b98b9b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-236890/selection/1a618d000210c17b3718f6e886c0c2f878226da4c6b1f8f0b9a530761419003f" :answer/id #uuid "84ff420b-cd3a-598b-be07-d84c30fdc42f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-236890/selection/6423513e171b5afa79ca48e931898185940a85ebaaf6dadd11a6f2d566c91a49" :answer/id #uuid "f6341528-c7b6-5399-8b52-720c78550729" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-236890/selection/dfa879c5187361c521910305b1d33c758fc2fbdab2d984242b7e043b37074919" :answer/id #uuid "a5cfdfd8-f2fb-5251-9ec2-7ccd0b9554cd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-236890/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "71e63e7f-f2ea-5901-8d3e-c21ff4233228" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-236890/selection/1a618d000210c17b3718f6e886c0c2f878226da4c6b1f8f0b9a530761419003f" :answer-field/choices ["q-236890/selection/d5383cc560f7210ce951b287d42180f2c52a051d33d7310f4c07703ce1cd1b4e" "q-236890/selection/dbaf85835946aefb97564ba0d1ea287b684a4c8821f4256502e349376df74d28" "q-236890/selection/1a618d000210c17b3718f6e886c0c2f878226da4c6b1f8f0b9a530761419003f" "q-236890/selection/6423513e171b5afa79ca48e931898185940a85ebaaf6dadd11a6f2d566c91a49" "q-236890/selection/dfa879c5187361c521910305b1d33c758fc2fbdab2d984242b7e043b37074919"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-236890" :question/id #uuid "7322d6d2-2ef7-599c-98ef-07bc2b13a18e" :question/math-academy-id "q-236890" :question/problem "Find the equation of the midline for a transformed sine function with a minimum value of $2$ and a maximum value of $10.$" :question/worked-solution "A sinusoidal graph's midline (or vertical shift) is the horizontal line that divides it vertically in half. \n\nThe equation of the midline is given by\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{{y}_{\\text{min}}+{y}_{\\text{max}}}{2},\n$$\n\nwhere ${y}_{\\text{min}}$ and ${y}_{\\text{max}}$ are the minimum and maximum values of the function. The midline equals the average of the maximum and minimum values. \n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{y}_{\\text{min}}+{y}_{\\text{max}}}{2} & =\\frac{2+10}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{2} \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the midline is $y=6.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-236890/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "933b20c7-323f-5443-9cf4-97e87fa2c6fc"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-236890"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-236896"] :question/worked-solution "A sinusoidal graph's midline (or vertical shift) is the horizontal line that divides it vertically in half. \n\nThe equation of the midline is given by\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{{y}_{\\text{min}}+{y}_{\\text{max}}}{2},\n$$\n\nwhere ${y}_{\\text{min}}$ and ${y}_{\\text{max}}$ are the minimum and maximum values of the function. The midline equals the average of the maximum and minimum values. \n\nIn 