ame{cos}⁡(3x+\\pi )\\le 1.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the above inequality by $-1$ and then subtracting $4,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1 & \\le \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x+\\pi )\\le 1 \\\\ 1 & \\ge -\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x+\\pi )\\ge -1 \\\\ -3 & \\ge -\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x+\\pi )-4\\ge -5 \\\\ -5 & \\le f(x)\\le -3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the minimum value is $-5.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-65928/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5696c2d5-4e35-5ed3-a4a2-6fe9b158e461"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-65928"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
